{"metadata":{"externalID":"s:8RcloneRC0A7ObscureO","title":"RcloneObscure","modules":[{"name":"RcloneRC"}],"symbolKind":"enum","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RcloneObscure","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RcloneObscure"}],"roleHeading":"Enumeration"},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"rclone’s reversible “obscure” encoding, done in process.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/docs.RcloneRC\/documentation\/RcloneRC"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RcloneObscure"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Rclone stores passwords in its config obscured, not encrypted: AES-256-CTR under a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"key published in rclone’s own source ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fs\/config\/obscure"},{"type":"text","text":"), with a random 16-byte"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"IV prepended and the result base64url-encoded without padding. Anyone with rclone"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can reverse it, which is the point — it only stops a password being read at a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"glance."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"grrclone used to reverse it by running "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rclone reveal -- <obscured>"},{"type":"text","text":", and that put"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the value on a command line. macOS lets every local account read every other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"account’s process arguments, and since obscuring is reversible, that was the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"plaintext credential in the process list for as long as the helper ran (#156)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rclone reveal"},{"type":"text","text":" cannot read stdin instead: given "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-"},{"type":"text","text":", it tries to decode "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Doing it here means the value never leaves this process."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Verified against rclone 1.75.1’s own ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"obscure"},{"text":" output in both directions, including","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"values that begin with a dash, Unicode, and the empty string; see ObscureTests.","type":"text"}]}]}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Methods","title":"Type Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/docs.RcloneRC\/documentation\/RcloneRC\/RcloneObscure\/obscure(_:)","doc:\/\/docs.RcloneRC\/documentation\/RcloneRC\/RcloneObscure\/reveal(_:)"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Enumerations","title":"Enumerations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/docs.RcloneRC\/documentation\/RcloneRC\/RcloneObscure\/Failure"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/docs.RcloneRC\/documentation\/RcloneRC\/RcloneObscure","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/rclonerc\/rcloneobscure"]}],"references":{"doc://docs.RcloneRC/documentation/RcloneRC":{"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/rclonerc","kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/docs.RcloneRC\/documentation\/RcloneRC","title":"RcloneRC","type":"topic"},"doc://docs.RcloneRC/documentation/RcloneRC/RcloneObscure/obscure(_:)":{"title":"obscure(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/rclonerc\/rcloneobscure\/obscure(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/docs.RcloneRC\/documentation\/RcloneRC\/RcloneObscure\/obscure(_:)","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"obscure","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Obscure a value as rclone would, with a fresh random IV. Used by tests to prove","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rclone reads back what this writes.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://docs.RcloneRC/documentation/RcloneRC/RcloneObscure":{"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RcloneObscure","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"rclone’s reversible “obscure” encoding, done in process.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RcloneObscure","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"RcloneObscure","role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/rclonerc\/rcloneobscure","identifier":"doc:\/\/docs.RcloneRC\/documentation\/RcloneRC\/RcloneObscure"},"doc://docs.RcloneRC/documentation/RcloneRC/RcloneObscure/reveal(_:)":{"title":"reveal(_:)","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"reveal","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/rclonerc\/rcloneobscure\/reveal(_:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The plaintext behind an obscured value."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/docs.RcloneRC\/documentation\/RcloneRC\/RcloneO